      "data": {
        "text": "**Developing the Core Function**\n\nI've got the `synthesize_ssml.py` script up and running. It leans on the Google Cloud Text-to-Speech library. I've successfully implemented the core function to generate SSML audio. The code imports the necessary modules and leverages the `TextToSpeechClient()`. I specified the `name` field for the voices.\n\n\n**Confirming Functional Implementation**\n\nI've verified that the `synthesize_ssml.py` file is complete. I've got the core function implemented, leveraging the Google Cloud Text-to-Speech library exactly as specified. Specifically, this code imports `google.cloud.texttospeech` and utilizes `texttospeech.TextToSpeechClient()`, and the `name` field for the voice, such as `en-US-Wavenet-D`, is specified. I've also provided example SSML with included prosody controls. This satisfies all the initial requirements.\n\n\n",
